* ngspice startup flags for this project. Only picked up if ngspice is
* invoked from this directory (or this file is copied alongside wherever
* it's run from) -- ngspice reads .spiceinit from the current directory,
* not the repo root implicitly.
*
* sky130A's combined model library takes ~2 minutes to parse regardless
* (confirmed upstream: https://github.com/iic-jku/IIC-OSIC-TOOLS/issues/262
* -- it's the library text parsing itself, not something these flags fix).
* These give a small, free improvement on top of that, nothing more.
*
* Do NOT add `set ngbehavior=hsa` here. It looks like a harmless HSPICE-
* compatibility toggle, but it changes ngspice's default element scale
* factor, which breaks automatic bin selection for the PDK's binned
* high-voltage FET models (sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5, used by
* mosbius_nmos.sch/mosbius_pmos.sch): every instance fails with "could not
* find a valid modelname" because its L falls outside every bin's
* [lmin,lmax] once the scale shifts. Found the hard way while getting the
* M5 example simulations to run at all -- confirmed by re-running with
* this line removed, which produces a normal transient solution instead.
set skywaterpdk
set ng_nomodcheck
set num_threads=8
option noinit
option klu
